dynamic_tools.description:
Execute a GraphQL query against the AT Explore API. Fetch multiple related pieces of data efficiently in a single call.

Root queries:
- profile(identifier: String!): Profile - unified entry point with protocol auto-detection (AT Protocol handle/DID or ActivityPub "user@instance.social")
- user(identifier: String!): User (deprecated — use profile())
- record(uri: String!) - AT Protocol record by AT URI
- apUser(handle: String!): APUser (deprecated — use profile())
- lexiconSchema(nsid: String!) - Lexicon schema by NSID
- verifications(handle?, subject?, limit?, cursor?) - Verification records
- verifiers(handle?, limit?, cursor?) - Trusted verifiers
- verifier(did: String!) - Single verifier by DID

Use introspection to discover available fields:
- { __type(name: "Profile") { fields { name type { name } } } }
- { __type(name: "User") { fields { name description type { name } } } }
- { __type(name: "Record") { fields { name description } } }
- { __type(name: "APUser") { fields { name description } } }

Examples:
- { profile(identifier: "user.bsky.social") { handle protocol displayName stats { followersCount } ... on ATProtoProfile { did } } }
- { profile(identifier: "user@mastodon.social") { handle protocol displayName stats { followersCount } ... on ActivityPubProfile { url } } }
- { user(identifier: "alice.bsky.social") { did, stats { followersCount, postsCount } } }
- { user(identifier: "alice.bsky.social") { records(collection: "app.bsky.feed.post", limit: 5) { records { uri, value } } } }
- { apUser(handle: "Gargron@mastodon.social") { displayName, stats { followersCount } } }
